Z||000003||Taijiguy||05-24-2001||10:43 PM||||This just hasn't been a good day. Now I think I've been ripped off for almost $600 by some jerk-off on ebay for a laptop. I had the high bid on a Sony VAIO 505. The guy had over 40 transactions, 39 positive feedbacks. But so far, he's lied to me twice in two days that I know of. Today i called him and he said he would send it overnight, and email me the tracking info. Needless to say, I haven't gotten an email from this scumbag. I wrote him a nasty-gram. My next email will be my last, then I'm pursuing all legal avenues available. Anyone here live in Charleston, and care to go collect my computer for me?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>||||reg||8
Z||000004||JSocha||05-25-2001||12:05 AM||||I got weather bug as well.  Mine gave me the option whether I wanted to install or not and I chose no on my home computer.<P>Didn't notice it the first time when I installed it at work.<P>This is what I did at work (which also sits behind a Firewall), Click on START &gt; RUN and type MSCONFIG and press ENTER.<P>Go to the STARTUP Tab and find anything related to GATOR and uncheck it.  Shouldn't pop up anymore.<P>I just checked my home computer and it is not installed, at least that I know of or can find.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||05-25-2001||12:10 AM||||I tried to run the uninstaller, and it wouldn't run. So I went through and eradicated it from my computer. Searched for Gator and wiped out all files. Then ran regedit and wiped it out of my registry. The install proggy is gone too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||05-25-2001||01:26 PM||||I'm not familiar with Gator, but if something is reappearing when you reboot, run regedit and look in the following for anything suspicious:<BR> HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run<P>Anything here gets run when you reboot (or logoff/logon in NT/2000)...<P>||||reg||1
